{
  "title": "Extract footnote text from recipe ingredients",
  "description": "Ingredient footnotes are lost during extraction.\n\
\n\
Many recipe sites use asterisks (*, **) on ingredients to reference footnotes \
with useful information like substitutions, brand recommendations, and \
technique tips (e.g., 'all-purpose flour*' with a footnote explaining \
multigrain alternatives, or 'kosher salt**' noting saltiness varies by brand). \
The asterisks survive into parsed item names but the footnote text itself is \
lost for most recipes: JSON-LD and microdata don't include it, and HTML \
fallback extraction sometimes captures it in instructions but doesn't link it \
to ingredients.\n\
\n\
We should extract footnote text and attach it to the corresponding ingredient, \
probably as a note. This would let us strip the asterisks from item names \
while preserving the information they reference.\n\
\n\
Affected pipeline fixtures include gimmesomeoven, smittenkitchen, \
cookingclassy, barefeetinthekitchen, sweetandsavorymeals, joyfoodsunshine, \
acouplecooks, loveandoliveoil, and others (~15+ items across ~10 recipes).",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 4,
  "type": "task",
  "labels": [
    "extraction",
    "ingredient-parser",
  ],
